-- Every night, rule SuspendMembers suspends each member that has no suspension yet, by creating
-- a Suspension for it. The Suspension it creates makes its own condition,
-- `not exists Suspension for this`, false for that member, and true for no other member.
--
-- `velle compare` from an empty spec (an empty file) to this file prints, under "What that
-- changes", these lines among others. Each is followed in the report by its "In the spec:"
-- lines, left out here.
--
--   ### Member
--   - A new Member can now cause SuspendMembers to run, later rather than in the same commit.
--   ### SuspendMembers
--   - SuspendMembers can now cause SuspendMembers to run, later rather than in the same commit.
--
-- The second line cannot happen: creating a Suspension can only take a member out of the rule's
-- condition, so the rule never causes itself to run. The first line is true.
act Member { name: text }

shape Suspension { member: one Member }

rule SuspendMembers when (Member where not exists Suspension for this) on Nightly {
    Suspension from { member: this }
}
